egers,\nand store the results in dst using zeromask k (elements are zeroed out if the corresponding bit is not set).\nRounding is done according to the ROUNDING parameter, which can be one of:\n\n* [`_MM_FROUND_TO_NEAREST_INT`] | [`_MM_FROUND_NO_EXC`] : round to nearest and suppress exceptions\n* [`_MM_FROUND_TO_NEG_INF`] | [`_MM_FROUND_NO_EXC`] : round down and suppress exceptions\n* [`_MM_FROUND_TO_POS_INF`] | [`_MM_FROUND_NO_EXC`] : round up and suppress exceptions\n* [`_MM_FROUND_TO_ZERO`] | [`_MM_FROUND_NO_EXC`] : truncate and suppress exceptions\n* [`_MM_FROUND_CUR_DIRECTION`] : use `MXCSR.RC` - see [`_MM_SET_ROUNDING_MODE`]\n\n[Intel's Documentation](https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/docs/intrinsics-guide/index.html#text=_mm512_maskz_cvt_roundpd_epu64&ig_expand=1480)","links":{"`_MM_FROUND_TO_POS_INF`":35150,"`_MM_SET_ROUNDING_MODE`":34890,"`_MM_FROUND_TO_NEAREST_INT`":35148,"`_MM_FROUND_NO_EXC`":35154,"`_MM_FROUND_TO_NEG_INF`":35149,"`_MM_FROUND_TO_ZERO`":35151,"`_MM_FROUND_CUR_DIRECTION`":35152},"attrs":[{"other":"#[<cfg_attr>(test, assert_instr(vcvtpd2uqq, ROUNDING = 8))]"},{"other":"#[rustc_legacy_const_generics(2)]"},{"other":"#[attr = Stability {stability: Stability {level: Stable {since: Version(RustcVersion {major: 1,\nminor: 89, patch: 0})}, feature: \"stdarch_x86_avx512\"}}]"},{"target_feature":{"enable":["avx512dq"]}},{"other":"#[attr = Inline(Hint)]"}],"deprecation":null,"inner":{"function":{"sig":{"inputs":[["k",{"resolved_path":{"path":"__mmask8","id":35780,"args":null}}],["a",{"resolved_path":{"path":"__m512d","id":9298,"args":null}}],["ROUNDING",{"primitive":"i32"}]],"output":{"resolved_path":{"path":"__m512i","id":9292,"args":null}},"is_c_variadic":false},"generics":{"params":[],"where_predicates":[]},"header":{"is_const":false,"is_unsafe":false,"is_async":false,"abi":"Rust"},"has_body":true}}},"21780":{"id":21780,"crate_id":0,"name":"sample","span":{"filename":"library\\core\\src\\random.rs","begin":[52,1],"end":[52,21]},"visibility":"