oundsd_ss","span":{"filename":"library\\core\\src\\..\\..\\stdarch\\crates\\core_arch\\src\\x86\\avx512f.rs","begin":[41237,1],"end":[41245,2]},"visibility":"public","docs":"Convert the lower double-precision (64-bit) floating-point element in b to a single-precision (32-bit) floating-point element, store the result in the lower element of dst, and copy the upper 3 packed elements from a to the upper elements of dst.\\\nRounding is done according to the rounding\\[3:0\\] parameter, which can be one of:\\\n* [`_MM_FROUND_TO_NEAREST_INT`] | [`_MM_FROUND_NO_EXC`] : round to nearest and suppress exceptions\n* [`_MM_FROUND_TO_NEG_INF`] | [`_MM_FROUND_NO_EXC`] : round down and suppress exceptions\n* [`_MM_FROUND_TO_POS_INF`] | [`_MM_FROUND_NO_EXC`] : round up and suppress exceptions\n* [`_MM_FROUND_TO_ZERO`] | [`_MM_FROUND_NO_EXC`] : truncate and suppress exceptions\n* [`_MM_FROUND_CUR_DIRECTION`] : use `MXCSR.RC` - see [`_MM_SET_ROUNDING_MODE`]\n\n[Intel's documentation](https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/docs/intrinsics-guide/index.html#text=mm_cvt_roundsd_ss&expand=1361)","links":{"`_MM_FROUND_TO_POS_INF`":35150,"`_MM_SET_ROUNDING_MODE`":34890,"`_MM_FROUND_TO_NEAREST_INT`":35148,"`_MM_FROUND_NO_EXC`":35154,"`_MM_FROUND_TO_NEG_INF`":35149,"`_MM_FROUND_TO_ZERO`":35151,"`_MM_FROUND_CUR_DIRECTION`":35152},"attrs":[{"other":"#[<cfg_attr>(test, assert_instr(vcvtsd2ss, ROUNDING = 8))]"},{"other":"#[rustc_legacy_const_generics(2)]"},{"other":"#[attr = Stability {stability: Stability {level: Stable {since: Version(RustcVersion {major: 1,\nminor: 89, patch: 0})}, feature: \"stdarch_x86_avx512\"}}]"},{"target_feature":{"enable":["avx512f"]}},{"other":"#[attr = Inline(Hint)]"}],"deprecation":null,"inner":{"function":{"sig":{"inputs":[["a",{"resolved_path":{"path":"__m128","id":9277,"args":null}}],["b",{"resolved_path":{"path":"__m128d","id":9280,"args":null}}],["ROUNDING",{"primitive":"i32"}]],"output":{"resolved_path":{"path":"__m128","id":9277,"args":null}},"is_c_variadic":