:27237,"crate_id":0,"name":null,"span":{"filename":"library\\core\\src\\any.rs","begin":[138,1],"end":[142,2]},"visibility":"default","docs":null,"links":{},"attrs":[],"deprecation":null,"inner":{"impl":{"is_unsafe":false,"generics":{"params":[{"name":"T","kind":{"type":{"bounds":[],"default":null,"is_synthetic":false}}}],"where_predicates":[{"bound_predicate":{"type":{"generic":"T"},"bounds":[{"outlives":"'static"},{"trait_bound":{"trait":{"path":"Sized","id":7,"args":null},"generic_params":[],"modifier":"maybe"}}],"generic_params":[]}}]},"provided_trait_methods":[],"trait":{"path":"Any","id":707,"args":null},"for":{"resolved_path":{"path":"RangeInclusive","id":8737,"args":{"angle_bracketed":{"args":[{"type":{"generic":"Idx"}}],"constraints":[]}}}},"items":[704],"is_negative":false,"is_synthetic":false,"blanket_impl":{"generic":"T"}}}},"49035":{"id":49035,"crate_id":0,"name":null,"span":{"filename":"library\\core\\src\\convert\\mod.rs","begin":[785,1],"end":[791,2]},"visibility":"default","docs":null,"links":{},"attrs":[],"deprecation":null,"inner":{"impl":{"is_unsafe":false,"generics":{"params":[{"name":"T","kind":{"type":{"bounds":[],"default":null,"is_synthetic":false}}}],"where_predicates":[]},"provided_trait_methods":[],"trait":{"path":"From","id":61,"args":{"angle_bracketed":{"args":[{"type":{"generic":"T"}}],"constraints":[]}}},"for":{"primitive":"f16"},"items":[693],"is_negative":false,"is_synthetic":false,"blanket_impl":{"generic":"T"}}}},"9290":{"id":9290,"crate_id":0,"name":null,"span":{"filename":"library\\core\\src\\..\\..\\stdarch\\crates\\core_arch\\src\\x86\\mod.rs","begin":[8,1],"end":[279,2]},"visibility":"default","docs":null,"links":{},"attrs":[{"other":"#[doc(cfg(any(target_arch = \"x86\", target_arch = \"x86_64\")))]"},{"other":"#[allow(non_camel_case_types)]"},{"other":"#[allow(clippy :: missing_inline_in_public_items)]"},{"other":"#[attr = Stability {stability: Stability {level: Stable {since: Version(RustcVersion {major: 1,\nminor: 27, patch: 0})}, feature: \"simd_x86\"}}]"},"automatically_derived"],"deprecation":null,"inner":{"impl":{"is_unsafe":false,"generics":{"params":[],"where_predicates":[]},"provided_trait_methods":["clone_from"],"trait":{"path":"Clone","id":37,"args":null},"for":{"resolved_path":{"path":"__m256d","id":9289,"args":null}},"items":[9288],"is_negative":false,"is_synthetic":false,"blanket_impl":null}}},"31088":{"id":31088,"crate_id":0,"name":"sm4ed","span":{"filename":"library\\core\\src\\..\\..\\stdarch\\crates\\core_arch\\src\\riscv_shared\\zk.rs","begin":[266,1],"end":[270,2]},"visibility":"public","docs":"Accelerates the block encrypt/decrypt operation of the SM4 block cipher \\[5, 31\\].\n\nImplements a T-tables in hardware style approach to accelerating the SM4 round function. A\nbyte is extracted from rs2 based on bs, to which the SBox and linear layer transforms are\napplied, before the result is XOR’d with rs1 and written back to rd. This instruction\nexists on RV32 and RV64 base architectures. On RV64, the 32-bit result is sign extended to\nXLEN bits. This instruction must always be implemented such that its execution latency does\nnot depend on the data being operated on.\n\nSource: RISC-V Cryptography Extensions Volume I: Scalar & Entropy Source Instructions\n\nVersion: v1.0.1\n\nSection: 3.43\n\n# Note\n\nThe `BS` parameter is expected to be a constant value and only the bottom 2 bits of `bs` are\nused.\n\n# Details\n\nAccelerates the round function `F` in the SM4 block cipher algorithm\n\nThis instruction is included in extension `Zksed`. It's defined as:\n\n```text\nSM4ED(x, a, BS) = x ⊕ T(ai)\n... where\nai = a.bytes[BS]\nT(ai) = L(τ(ai))\nbi = τ(ai) = SM4-S-Box(ai)\nci = L(bi) = bi ⊕ (bi ≪ 2) ⊕ (bi ≪ 10) ⊕ (bi ≪ 18) ⊕ (bi ≪ 24)\nSM4ED = (ci ≪ (BS * 8)) ⊕ x\n```\n\nwhere `⊕` represents 32-bit xor, and `≪ k` represents rotate left by `k` bits.\nAs is defined above, `T` is a combined transformation of non linear S-Box transform `τ`\nand linear layer transform `L`.\n\nIn the SM4 algorithm, the round function `F` is defined as:\n\n```text\nF(x0, x1, x2, x3, rk) = x0 ⊕ T(x1 ⊕ x2 ⊕ x3 ⊕ rk)\n... where\nT(A) = L(τ(A))\nB = τ(A) = (SM4-S-Box(a0), SM4-S-Box(a1), SM4-S-Box(a2), SM4-S-Box(a3))\nC = L(B) = B ⊕ (B ≪ 2) ⊕ (B ≪ 10) ⊕ (B ≪ 18) ⊕ (B ≪ 24)\n```\n\nIt can be implemented by `sm4ed` instruction like:\n\n```no_run\n# #[cfg(any(target_arch = \"riscv32\", target_arch = \"riscv64\"))]\n# fn round_function(x0: u32, x1: u32, x2: u32, x3: u32, rk: u32) -> u32 {\n# #[cfg(target_arch = \"riscv32\")] use core::arch::riscv32::sm4ed;\n# #[cfg(target_arch = \"riscv64\")] use core::arch::riscv64::sm4ed;\nlet a = x1 ^ x2 ^ x3 ^ rk;\nlet c0 = sm4ed(x0, a, 0);\nlet c1 = sm4ed(c0, a, 1); // c1 represents c[0..=1], etc.\nlet c2 = sm4ed(c1, a, 2);\nlet c3 = sm4ed(c2, a, 3);\nreturn c3; // c3 represents c[0..=3]\n# }\n```","links":{},"attrs":[{"other":"#[rustc_legacy_const_generics(2)]"},{"other":"#[<cfg_attr>(test, assert_instr(sm4ed, BS = 0))]"},{"other":"#[attr = Stability {stability: Stability {level: Unstable {reason: None,\nissue: 114544, is_soft: false}, feature: \"riscv_ext_intrinsics\"}}]"},{"target_feature":{"enable":["zksed"]}},{"other":"#[attr = Inline(Hint)]"}],"deprecation":null,"inner":{"function":{"sig":{"inputs":[["rs1",{"primitive":"u32"}],["rs2",{"primitive":"u32"}],["BS",{"primitive":"u8"}]],"output":{"primitive":"u32"},"is_c_variadic":false},"generics":{"params":[],"where_predicates":[]},"header":{"is_const":false,"is_unsafe":false,"is_async":false,"abi":"Rust"},"has_body":true}}},"13141":{"id":13141,"crate_id":0,"name":null,"span":null,"visibility":"default","docs":null,"links":{},"attrs":[],"deprecation":null,"inner":{"impl":{"is_unsafe":false,"generics":{"params":[{"name":"'a","kind":{"lifetime":{"outlives":[]}}},{"name":"T","kind":{"type":{"bounds":[],"default":null,"is_synthetic":false}}}],"where_predicates":[]},"provided_trait_methods":[],"trait":{"path":"Freeze","id":676,"args":null},"for":{"resolved_path":{"path":"IterMut","id":11935,"args":{"angle_bracketed":{"args":[{"lifetime":"'a"},{"type":{"generic":"T"}}],"constraints":[]}}}},"items":[],"is_negative":false,"is_synthetic":true,"blanket_impl":null}}},"34939":{"id":34939,"crate_id":0,"name":"_mm_slli_epi32","span":{"filename":"library\\core\\src\\..\\..\\stdarch\\crates\\core_arch\\src\\x86\\sse2.rs","begin":[565,1],"end":[574,2]},"visibility":"public","docs":"Shifts packed 32-bit integers in `a` left by `IMM8` while shifting in zeros.\n\n[Intel's documentation](https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/docs/intrinsics-guide/index.html#text=_mm_slli_epi32)","links":{},"attrs":[{"other":"#[<cfg_attr>(test, assert_instr(pslld, IMM8 = 7))]"},{"other":"#[rustc_legacy_const_generics(1)]"},{"other":"#[attr = Stability {stability: Stability {level: Stable {since: Version(RustcVersion {major: 1,\nminor: 27, patch: 0})}, feature: \"simd_x86\"}}]"},{"target_feature":{"enable":["sse2"]}},{"other":"#[attr = Inline(Hint)]"}],"deprecation":null,"inner":{"function":{"sig":{"inputs":[["a",{"resolved_path":{"path":"__m128i","id":9274,"args":null}}],["IMM8",{"primitive":"i32"}]],"output":{"resolved_path":{"path":"__m128i","id":9274,"args":null}},"is_c_variadic":false},"generics":{"params":[],"where_predicates":[]},"header":{"is_const":false,"is_unsafe":false,"is_async":false,"abi":"Rust"},"has_body":true}}},"16992":{"id":16992,"crate_id":0,"name":"Output","span":{"filename":"library\\core\\src\\ops\\bit.rs","begin":[517,1],"end":[517,70]},"visibility":"default","docs":null,"links":{},"attrs":[],"deprecation":null,"inner":{"assoc_type":{"generics":{"params":[],"where_predicates":[]},"bounds":[],"type":{"qualified_path":{"name":"Output","args":null,"self_type":{"primitive":"u128"},"trait":{"path":"Shl","id":4632,"args":{"angle_bracketed":{"args":[{"type":{"primitive":"u8"}}],"constraints":[]}}}}}}}},"38790":{"id":38790,"crate_id":0,"name":"_mm_maskz_max_epu16","span":{"filename":"library\\core\\src\\..\\..\\stdarch\\crates\\core_arch\\src\\x86\\avx512