ngle_bracketed":{"args":[{"type":{"resolved_path":{"path":"Duration","id":8927,"args":null}}}],"constraints":[]}}},"for":{"primitive":"u32"},"items":[14599,14600],"is_negative":false,"is_synthetic":false,"blanket_impl":null}}},"36399":{"id":36399,"crate_id":0,"name":"_mm512_roundscale_round_pd","span":{"filename":"library\\core\\src\\..\\..\\stdarch\\crates\\core_arch\\src\\x86\\avx512f.rs","begin":[10196,1],"end":[10204,2]},"visibility":"public","docs":"Round packed double-precision (64-bit) floating-point elements in a to the number of fraction bits specified by imm8, and store the results in dst.\\\nRounding is done according to the imm8\\[2:0\\] parameter, which can be one of:\\\n* [`_MM_FROUND_TO_NEAREST_INT`] : round to nearest\n* [`_MM_FROUND_TO_NEG_INF`] : round down\n* [`_MM_FROUND_TO_POS_INF`] : round up\n* [`_MM_FROUND_TO_ZERO`] : truncate\n* [`_MM_FROUND_CUR_DIRECTION`] : use `MXCSR.RC` - see [`_MM_SET_ROUNDING_MODE`]\n\nExceptions can be suppressed by passing _MM_FROUND_NO_EXC in the sae parameter.\n[Intel's documentation](https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/docs/intrinsics-guide/index.html#text=_mm512_roundscale_round_pd&expand=4787)","links":{"`_MM_FROUND_TO_POS_INF`":35150,"`_MM_SET_ROUNDING_MODE`":34890,"`_MM_FROUND_TO_NEAREST_INT`":35148,"`_MM_FROUND_CUR_DIRECTION`":35152,"`_MM_FROUND_TO_NEG_INF`":35149,"`_MM_FROUND_TO_ZERO`":35151},"attrs":[{"other":"#[<cfg_attr>(test, assert_instr(vrndscalepd, IMM8 = 0, SAE = 8))]"},{"other":"#[rustc_legacy_const_generics(1, 2)]"},{"other":"#[attr = Stability {stability: Stability {level: Stable {since: Version(RustcVersion {major: 1,\nminor: 89, patch: 0})}, feature: \"stdarch_x86_avx512\"}}]"},{"target_feature":{"enable":["avx512f"]}},{"other":"#[attr = Inline(Hint)]"}],"deprecation":null,"inner":{"function":{"sig":{"inputs":[["a",{"resolved_path":{"path":"__m512d","id":9298,"args":null}}],["IMM8",{"primitive":"i32"}],["SAE",{"primitive":"i32"}]],"output":{"resolved_path":{"path":"__m512d","id":9298,"args":null}},"is_c_variadic":false},"generics":{"params":[],"where_predicates":[]},"header":{"is_const":false,"is_unsafe":false,"is_async":false,"abi":"Rust"},"has_body":true}}},"18452":{"id":18452,"crate_id":0,"name":"Output","span":{"filename":"library\\core\\src\\ops\\bit.rs","begin":[639,1],"end":[639,70]},"visibility":"default","docs":null,"links":{},"attrs":[],"deprecation":null,"inner":{"assoc_type":{"generics":{"params":[],"where_predicates":[]},"bounds":[],"type":{"primitive":"u16"}}}},"40250":{"id":40250,"crate_id":0,"name":"_mm256_mask_gf2p8affineinv_epi64_epi8","span":{"filename":"library\\core\\src\\..\\..\\stdarch\\crates\\core_arch\\src\\x86\\gfni.rs","begin":[636,1],"end":[650,2]},"visibility":"public","docs":"Performs an affine transformation on the inverted packed bytes in x.\nThat is computes a*inv(x)+b over the Galois Field 2^8 for each packed byte with a being a 8x8 bit matrix\nand b being a constant 8-bit immediate value.\nThe inverse of a byte is defined with respect to the reduction polynomial x^8+x^4+x^3+x+1.\nThe inverse of 0 is 0.\nEach pack of 8 bytes in x is paired with the 64-bit word at the same position in a.\n\nUses the writemask in k - elements are copied from src if the corresponding mask bit is not set.\nOtherwise the computation result is written into the result.\n\n[Intel's documentation](https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/docs/intrinsics-guide/index.html#text=_mm256_mask_gf2p8affineinv_epi64_epi8)","links":{},"attrs":[{"other":"#[<cfg_attr>(test, assert_instr(vgf2p8affineinvqb, B = 0))]"},{"other":"#[rustc_legacy_const_generics(4)]"},{"other":"#[attr = Stability {stability: Stability {level: Stable {since: Version(RustcVersion {major: 1,\nminor: 89, patch: 0})}, feature: \"stdarch_x86_avx512\"}}]"},{"target_feature":{"enable":["gfni","avx512bw","avx512vl"]}},{"other":"#[attr = Inline(Hint)]"}],"deprecation":null,"inner":{"function":{"sig":{"inputs":[["src",{"resolved_path":{"path":"crate::core_arch::x86::__m256i","id":9283,"args