particular, a debugger may be able to resume execution.\n\nIf possible, this will produce an instruction sequence that allows a debugger to resume *after*\nthe breakpoint, rather than resuming *at* the breakpoint; however, the exact behavior is\ntarget-specific and debugger-specific, and not guaranteed.\n\nIf the target platform does not have any kind of debug breakpoint instruction, this may compile\nto a trapping instruction (e.g. an undefined instruction) instead, or to some other form of\ntarget-specific abort that may or may not support convenient resumption.\n\nThe precise behavior and the precise instruction generated are not guaranteed, except that in\nnormal execution with no debug tooling involved this will not continue executing.\n\n- On x86 targets, this produces an `int3` instruction.\n- On aarch64 targets, this produces a `brk #0xf000` instruction.","links":{},"attrs":[{"other":"#[attr = Stability {stability: Stability {level: Unstable {reason: None,\nissue: 133724, is_soft: false}, feature: \"breakpoint\"}}]"},{"other":"#[attr = Inline(Always)]"}],"deprecation":null,"inner":{"function":{"sig":{"inputs":[],"output":null,"is_c_variadic":false},"generics":{"params":[],"where_predicates":[]},"header":{"is_const":false,"is_unsafe":false,"is_async":false,"abi":"Rust"},"has_body":true}}},"7045":{"id":7045,"crate_id":0,"name":"bitor","span":{"filename":"library\\core\\src\\num\\wrapping.rs","begin":[566,1],"end":[566,71]},"visibility":"default","docs":null,"links":{},"attrs":[{"other":"#[attr = Inline(Hint)]"},{"other":"#[attr = TrackCaller]"}],"deprecation":null,"inner":{"function":{"sig":{"inputs":[["self",{"generic":"Self"}],["other",{"borrowed_ref":{"lifetime":null,"is_mutable":false,"type":{"resolved_path":{"path":"Wrapping","id":4335,"args":{"angle_bracketed":{"args":[{"type":{"primitive":"i128"}}],"constraints":[]}}}}}}]],"output":{"qualified_path":{"name":"Output","args":null,"self_type":{"resolved_path":{"path":"Wrapping","id":4335,"args":{"angle_bra