I character from the byte `b`,\nwithout checking whether it's valid.\n\n# Safety\n\n`b` must be in `0..=127`, or else this is UB.","links":{},"attrs":[{"other":"#[attr = Stability {stability: Stability {level: Unstable {reason: None,\nissue: 110998, is_soft: false}, feature: \"ascii_char\"}}]"},{"other":"#[attr = Inline(Hint)]"}],"deprecation":null,"inner":{"function":{"sig":{"inputs":[["b",{"primitive":"u8"}]],"output":{"generic":"Self"},"is_c_variadic":false},"generics":{"params":[],"where_predicates":[]},"header":{"is_const":true,"is_unsafe":true,"is_async":false,"abi":"Rust"},"has_body":true}}},"44393":{"id":44393,"crate_id":0,"name":"vec_srv","span":{"filename":"library\\core\\src\\..\\..\\stdarch\\crates\\core_arch\\src\\powerpc\\altivec.rs","begin":[3519,1],"end":[3521,2]},"visibility":"public","docs":"Vector Shift Right Variable\n\n## Result value\nLet v be a 17-byte vector formed from a zero byte in element 0 and the elements of\na in bytes `[1:16]`. Then each byte element i of r is determined as follows. The start bit sb is\nobtained from bits 5:7 of byte element i of b. Then the contents of bits (8 – sb):(15 – sb) of\nthe halfword in byte elements i:i+1 of v are placed into byte element i of r.\n\n## Endian considerations\nAll bit and byte element numbers are specified in big-endian order. This intrinsic is not\nendian-neutral.","links":{},"attrs":[{"other":"#[attr = Stability {stability: Stability {level: Unstable {reason: None,\nissue: 111145, is_soft: false}, feature: \"stdarch_powerpc\"}}]"},{"target_feature":{"enable":["power9-altivec"]}},{"other":"#[attr = Inline(Hint)]"}],"deprecation":null,"inner":{"function":{"sig":{"inputs":[["a",{"resolved_path":{"path":"vector_unsigned_char","id":9355,"args":null}}],["b",{"resolved_path":{"path":"vector_unsigned_char","id":9355,"args":null}}]],"output":{"resolved_path":{"path":"vector_unsigned_char","id":9355,"args":null}},"is_c_variadic":false},"generics":{"params":[],"where_predicates":[]},"header":{"is_cons